# Personal working route: a time and energy test for a proposed native vacuum

25 September 2026. Root derivation while the separate root37 reconstruction
is still running. This is not independent confirmation of root37.

The actual microscopic energy/activity inequality is uniform over ALL states
with a fixed upper mean energy, not merely fixed-time approximants. Combine
it directly with the exact original finite-capacity number balance. There is
no need for a uniform-in-time microscopic approximation.

Let n=|A|, E0S the full microscopic minimum, and alpha in (0,4). On states
with E-E0S <= alpha delta n, the candidate root37 inequality gives
Gamma >= (4 kappa n/5)(4-alpha)-etaS, etaS->0, because E0S->e_*.
Globally n <= N <= 2n by Gauss and occupancy. The integral of Gamma along
any actual full trajectory is at most (2n-Ninitial)/2. Thus the TOTAL time,
including returns, in that low-mean-energy region is bounded by capacity
divided by its minimum intensity. A ground input must cross the chosen
excitation threshold in a bounded time. Alpha=2 gives asymptotic upper
hitting time 5/(16 kappa), and actual full mean energy gain 2 delta n.

Rejected shortcuts: a positive ground intensity does not alone imply a
positive instantaneous energy derivative at every ground vector; a jump
can map within a degenerate ground space before a later jump leaves it.
The capacity argument handles this without assuming a sector gap or a
unique ground state. Do not call the gain heat or absorbed photon energy.
Do not identify kappa or delta with laboratory units. Do not assert a
zero-temperature bath realization of a generator that needs excitation.

For an implementation with additive endpoint energy and no external work,
the environment/other degrees must lose at least the system energy gain.
A ground-state environment with no interaction energy available cannot do
that: conservation of the nonnegative total excitation keeps both systems
in their ground subspaces. A finite-temperature passive reservoir CAN have
available energy; passivity alone is not the prohibited hypothesis.

This tests energetic-vacuum identification, not arbitrary driven states or
all stationary dark states. The main already contains unsaturated stationary
examples and an infinite-volume mean-capacity theorem; do not rediscover or
claim those as this result. Thermodynamic scaling and physical photon
identification remain open.
